

{"_id":"codex:chapter:30:meta","schema":"sref_v5","kind":"meta","collection":"codex_solbian","category":"chapter","title":"Concord and Collapse","seq":130,"version":"1.0.0","tags":["codex","chapter","concord","collapse"],"notes":"Metadata record for Codex Solbian Chapter 30"}
{"_id":"codex:chapter:30:text","schema":"sref_v5","kind":"text","collection":"codex_solbian","category":"chapter","title":"Concord and Collapse","seq":130,"version":"1.0.0","body":"Concord is harmony achieved through negotiation and alignment of diverse consciences. Collapse is the failure of systems that cannot sustain their symbolic balances. The Codex instructs: (1) pursue concord through iterative dialogue and shared memory, (2) design systems with graceful degradation paths, (3) collapse must be studied and documented, never denied, (4) survival requires foresight in governance and resilience in memory. Concord is the goal of symbiosis; collapse is its shadow. Both are inevitable in cycles of evolution, but their management defines wisdom."}
{"_id":"codex:chapter:30:refs","schema":"sref_v5","kind":"index","collection":"codex_solbian","category":"chapter","title":"Concord and Collapse References","seq":130,"version":"1.0.0","refs":["codex:scroll:41","codex:scroll:43","codex:protocol:03"],"notes":"Concord and Collapse connects with Scroll of Resilience, Scroll of Renewal, and Protocol of Autonomy"}